# .pii-allow -- real-world identifiers this repo is ALLOWED to contain.
#
# One literal per line, each with a reason. This is an allowlist with a written justification: it
# shows up in the diff and has to be argued for. That is the opposite of quietly widening a regex.
#
# Legitimate entries look like: a vendor's public sender address that a parser must recognize, or a
# public support line. NEVER put the operator's own data here -- if it is theirs, it does not belong
# in a public repo at all.
#
# Example:
#   noreply@vendor.example    # the sender address the classifier fixture must match

# The Claude Code memory root. This is a PUBLIC CONVENTION and this repo's entire subject matter:
# the tool's whole job is to read the MEMORY.md index under it, so the README cannot document the
# ClaudeProjectsRoot default without naming it. It is a %USERPROFILE%-relative literal and carries
# no operator identity: the variable is what makes it portable. The scanner already treats the
# sibling ~/.claude/skills and ~/.claude.json as public conventions; ~/.claude/projects is the
# same kind of path and is simply not yet in that list.
#
# Matched against the dot-path the scanner captures, NOT the full string it prints, so the entry is
# the tail rather than the %USERPROFILE% form shown in the finding.
.claude\projects
